00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:15.010
So, how can a Master or
especially an MBA help you

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:18.350
to transition into the career
that you really want to

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:19.960
if the job that you're currently doing

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:21.826
or the work experience that
you're currently having

00:02:21.826 --> 00:02:24.265
is just not what you really wanna do

00:02:24.265 --> 00:02:27.080
or maybe you're already
working in a specific function,

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.040
maybe in finance for several years

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.118
and you're just not sure how to transition

00:02:31.118 --> 00:02:33.597
and you're just not sure
how to move from there

00:02:33.597 --> 00:02:36.050
into completely other
role that you wanna do?

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:38.070
And here, yes, an MBA can help you

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:40.096
because with the MBA,
you have the opportunity

00:02:40.096 --> 00:02:43.550
to do that at a very prestigious program.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:45.160
So if you wanna do that and you feel like

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:48.110
your current academic performance
maybe regard to grades,

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:49.970
but maybe also the university itself

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:52.610
maybe isn't as great
as you would wish for,

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:54.741
here with the MBA, you
have the opportunity

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:57.900
to now aim for a good and
highly prestigious program.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:58.733
And if you're asking yourself,

00:02:58.733 --> 00:03:01.287
"Well, what are the most
prestigious programs,

00:03:01.287 --> 00:03:03.410
"what are the best MBA
