00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:33.290
But let's just assume that an MBA

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:35.560
or also a Master program
really can help you

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.670
to make this career transition, especially

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:38.880
if you're doing this with one of

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.600
the most highly-ranked programs out there.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:42.327
But now, of course,
you might ask yourself,

00:03:42.327 --> 00:03:44.990
"Well, how do I get into
these MBA programs?"

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:47.700
So you maybe know that
I did my MBA at INSEAD

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.677
and now you might ask, "Well,
how do I get into INSEAD

00:03:49.677 --> 00:03:51.177
"or into any of these programs,

00:03:51.177 --> 00:03:53.597
"especially if maybe
my academic performance

00:03:53.597 --> 00:03:56.157
"so far wasn't that amazing or maybe also

00:03:56.157 --> 00:03:58.507
"the work experience
that I have done so far

00:03:58.507 --> 00:04:00.037
"wasn't maybe there as probably

00:04:00.037 --> 00:04:01.810
"these top programs can expect?"

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:04.620
And this is now where
the GMAT comes into play

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:07.040
and I know there is lots of
controversy around the GMAT.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:09.170
Many people think that
it's just unnecessary,

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:11.190
that this is just an
annoyance that you need to do

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:13.060
to get into these programs, but I believe

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:15.970
the GMAT in may ways is an equalizer

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:18.374
and the reason for that
is that a high GMAT score

00:04:18.374 --> 00:04:22.690
can very much overcompensate
many of other drawbacks

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:25.130
of your application profile
that you might have.

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:27.320
So even if your grades
maybe weren't that great,

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.690
maybe the work experience
that you have wasn't

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:32.900
that impressive, if your
GMAT score is really high,

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:35.520
this can overcompensate
many of these things.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:38.140
So it can help you to level
the playing ground for you

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:41.040
to give you a true and
real shot into one of

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:43.180
the most competitive
MBA programs out there.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:45.040
So why do these top business schools put

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:46.730
so much emphasis on the GMAT?

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:49.290
And probably the main reason
is that the GMAT score,

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:52.030
the average GMAT score of the class is

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:55.620
a quality signal for the
quality of this MBA program.

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:59.170
So many MBA rankings, the
average or the mean GMAT score

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:01.640
of a class is a factor in that ranking,

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:03.440
so if an MBA program has more people

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.610
with high GMAT scores, this can help them

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.110
to score high in the GMAT.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.960
And from the perspective of a candidate,

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:11.210
if you wanna apply for MBA programs,

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.667
you know, check out all these GMAT scores,

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:14.500
and you were able to score high,

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.670
of course, you'd rather
wanna be in a class

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.520
with lots of other people who scored high

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:20.490
on the GMAT as well because the GMAT is

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:22.380
a good proxy for how well you will be able

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:23.980
to perform in a business context

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:26.510
and it is also correlated
with future career success.

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:28.640
This is exactly how the GMAT was set up,

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:30.840
why people developed the
GMAT in the first place.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:33.360
So put lots of preparation into your GMAT

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:36.330
to score as high as possible
and if you score high,

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:38.250
this can really help you to get into one

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:41.096
of the most selective MBA
programs and if you're doing

00:05:41.096 --> 00:05:43.498
one of these very
prestigious MBA programs,

00:05:43.498 --> 00:05:46.810
this can help you
significantly in your career

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:48.960
and then also to do all
kinds of career transitions

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:50.960
that you might wanna do, but
do not get me wrong here.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:53.300
Of course, I'm very well
aware that scoring high

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.920
on the GMAT is not easy
and I made a whole video

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.546
about how I prepared for the GMAT,

00:05:57.546 --> 00:05:59.370
the tips and tricks and strategies

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:02.505
that I used to score above
700 on my personal GMAT exam.

00:06:02.505 --> 00:06:04.050
If you haven't seen that yet,

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.470
also I have it included
here in a link above.

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:07.303
Check it out.

00:06:07.303 --> 00:06:08.490
So yes, of course, it's not easy.

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:10.910
It's not easy to get
into the most selective,

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:13.010
most prestigious MBA
programs of the world,

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:14.670
but the point that I just wanna stress is

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:16.847
that the GMAT can really
help you to overcome

00:06:16.847 --> 00:06:20.000
many weaknesses of your
profile of the past.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:22.471
With a high GMAT, of
course, there's no guarantee

00:06:22.471 --> 00:06:24.700
to get into all kinds of MBA programs,

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:26.370
but it will be a big help.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:28.070
So if you're looking
to do that transition,

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:30.040
do an MBA and try to get an MBA

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:33.410
that is as selective, as
competitive as possible

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:35.175
in terms of the rankings,
and to get in there,

00:06:35.175 --> 00:06:38.750
do a GMAT and try to score as
high as possible to get in.

